COPY from-spec to-spec

Copies files. The target must not exist yet. With wildcards, to-spec
may name a folder, such as [.BACKUP], or use * for the name or the type.

Qualifiers:
  /LOG      names each file copied
  /CONFIRM  asks before each file: Y yes, N no, A all, Q quit

Ctrl-C stops the copy. A file cut short is not left behind.

Example:
  COPY *.TXT [.BACKUP] /LOG
